    "analysis_type": "paradigm_network",
    "rationale": "A fully flat lexicon would be too conservative because several families show true substitution in a shared frame with compositionally stable parts: (i) Pm/Ps/Pf/Palt = 'patterns' + contrasting pattern states; (ii) H!/H?/Hw/H-/H0/Hq/Hr/Hz = 'hum/audio' + contrasting auditory qualities; (iii) smaller visual families C+/C-, Eo/E-/E~, Fo/F-/F+/Ff each show a fixed region/domain morpheme plus a contrasting state slot. I reject the suggested F- family from F-ok/F-rim- because ok and rim- do not form a coherent substituting class with predictable compositional meanings. I also leave many lookalikes lexical (e.g. T+/T-, ok+, K+, wrong+, H-thin, Hth) because no stable cross-entry paradigm makes their parts predictive.",
